<problem>
<!-- <title>Definite integral &#x2D; 1/x</title> -->

<setup>

<selectFromSequence name="aa" from="1" to="10" />
<selectFromSequence name="bb" from="-10" to="10" exclude="0" />
<math name="cc" simplify="numbers">$bb /$aa </math>
<function name="g" variables="t"><math simplify="true">$cc /t</math></function>
<selectFromSequence name="lb" from="1" to="4" />
<selectFromSequence name="ub" from="$lb+1" to="6" />

<function name="antideriv_g" variables="t" simplify="true" symbolic="true">$cc ln(|t|)</function>
<math name="intgeval" simplify="numbers">
  $$antideriv_g($ub) - $$antideriv_g($lb)
</math>

</setup>

<p>
Evaluate the following integral:</p>
  
<p><m>\displaystyle \int_{$lb}^{$ub} $g \, dt  =</m> 
<answer forceFullCheckworkButton="true" name="answer1">
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="true">$intgeval </award>
<award allowedErrorInNumbers="0.0001" credit="0.8" name="award1">$intgeval </award>
<award credit="0.64" allowedErrorInNumbers="0.001" feedbackCodes="numericalerror" name="award2">$intgeval </award>
</answer>
</p>
<feedback condition="$award1 or $award2">Don't round. Leave fractions as fractions and use ln().</feedback>
$answer1.feedbacks

<p>

For full credit, do not round your answer to a decimal.  (Maximum of 80% credit will be awarded for rounded answers that include at least 5 correct significant digits.)
</p>

<solution>


<p>
We first use the constant product rule for integrals to simplify:
</p>

<p>
<m>\displaystyle \int_{$lb}^{$ub} $g \, dt = $cc \int_{$lb}^{$ub} \frac{1}{t} dt</m>
</p>
<p>
Recall that the integral of one over  <m>t</m> is the natural logarithm of the absolute value of <m>t</m>:
</p>
  
<p>
<m>\displaystyle \int_{$lb}^{$ub} \frac{1}{t} dt = \ln(|t|)\bigg|_{$lb}^{$ub}  = <math simplify="true">ln(|$ub|)</math> - <math simplify="true">ln(|$lb|)</math> </m>
</p>
<p>
Multiplying by <m>$cc </m> gives us our final solution:
</p>
  
<p>
<m>\displaystyle $cc \left(<math simplify="true">ln(|$ub|)</math> - <math simplify="true">ln(|$lb|)</math>  \right)</m>
</p>

</solution>


</problem>